class:: GbmanMap
summary:: Trigger-driven raw Gingerbreadman map coordinates
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic>Maps
related:: Guides/Stochastica, Classes/GbmanSonify, Classes/HenonMap

description::

The Gingerbreadman map is a two-dimensional, piecewise-linear chaotic map. Its recurrence relation uses absolute values, causing state coordinates to jump discontinuously across a bounded region, forming a fractal shape resembling a gingerbread man. Conceptually, this piecewise nature means the trajectory does not flow smoothly; it snaps and zig-zags erratically. This makes it highly useful for generating glitchy, aggressive, stepped modulation or abrupt rhythmic triggers where continuous movement is undesirable.

Iterates the Gingerbreadman recurrence code::x' = 1 - y + abs(x):: and code::y' = x::. This explicit equation avoids ambiguity among map variants and is shared with link::Classes/GbmanSonify::.

The outputs are raw state coordinates. They are not normalized audio signals and may diverge for some parameters.

Like link::Classes/Stepper::, GbmanMap advances on trigger edges and holds; unlike Stepper, its state is a two-coordinate nonlinear recurrence.

subsection:: State-space portrait

image::gbman-map-phase.png#The default Gingerbreadman orbit after its transient. x is horizontal and y is vertical; points are iterations, not a continuous trajectory.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: trig
Advance on a rising edge.
argument:: x0
Initial x coordinate, sampled at construction and reset.
argument:: y0
Initial y coordinate, sampled at construction and reset.
argument:: reset
Restore initial state on a rising edge.
Returns:: Two audio-rate outputs: x and y.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments and outputs.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ GbmanMap.ar(Impulse.ar(40))[1] * 0.02 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ Pan2.ar(Decay2.ar(Impulse.ar(8), 0.001, 0.08), GbmanMap.kr(Impulse.kr(8))[0].fold2) * 0.1 }.play
)
::

code::
// Industrial Glitch Sequencer
(
{
    var trig, coords, freq, sig, filt, env;
    trig = Dust.kr(15);
    coords = GbmanMap.kr(trig);
    // Jagged piecewise jumps mapped to intense filter cutoff and noise bursts
    freq = coords[0].linexp(-2, 2, 100, 8000);
    sig = WhiteNoise.ar(0.5) + LPF.ar(Impulse.ar(coords[1].linlin(-2, 2, 1, 50)), 1000);
    filt = RLPF.ar(sig, freq, 0.1);
    env = EnvGen.kr(Env.perc(0.01, 0.05), trig);
    Pan2.ar(filt * env * 0.5, coords[1])
}.play;
)
::




subsection:: Real-time phase portrait

code::
(
SDPhaseView.open(
    "Gingerbreadman map: x-y phase portrait",
    [-4, 8], [-4, 8],
    { GbmanMap.kr(Impulse.kr(45)) },
    { |state|
        Pan2.ar(
            SinOsc.ar(state[0].clip(-4, 8).linexp(-4, 8, 100, 1800), 0, 0.06),
            state[1].clip(-4, 8).linlin(-4, 8, -1, 1)
        )
    }
);
)
::
